<StudyLayout>
  <section>
    <h2>Stellar characters — question review of 01</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/lab/studies/stellar-characters-2026-11-11"
        >Return to the study</a
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      Tested on 11 November 2026 by a clean-context, read-only reviewer with no
      part in framing and no expected result. This tests whether the question is
      answerable, not the quality of a design or its gameplay.
    </p>
    <h3>One subject / Pass after correction and recheck</h3>
    <p>
      The initial result was Fail: the earlier stellar-encounters study remains
      open and its question overlaps this one. Colour, surface and surrounding
      activity can be shown as one stellar identity; concurrent ownership was
      the issue. Section 01 now explicitly supersedes that earlier inquiry for
      stellar identity and states that its registry status creates neither a
      dependency nor a second owner. The earlier record and status are
      preserved. The reviewer rechecked the corrected wording on 11 November
      2026 and confirmed that the ownership finding is resolved.
    </p>
    <h3>Grounded / Pass</h3>
    <p>
      The standard Sun’s collection, pull, exposure and lethal contact exist in
      the star spec and production code. Current handling and the procedural,
      high-contrast art direction have standing specifications. Candidates are
      research prompts; proposed mechanics remain hypotheses. Close views,
      flight-scale compositions and sequences can show visual communication.
    </p>
    <h3>Consequence / Pass</h3>
    <p>
      The answer changes stellar encounters’ visible identities: colour, surface
      and activity would suggest different opportunities and dangers before a
      pilot approaches. Survival balance is outside this communication claim.
    </p>
    <h3>Grounding evidence</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Standard Sun: <code>docs/specs/game/world/star/spec.md</code>, Intent
        and Contract; <code>packages/core/src/lib/solar.ts</code>;
        <code>packages/core/src/lib/physics/Physics.ts</code>, collection, hull
        updates and mass wells;
        <code>packages/mode-a/src/lib/simulation.ts</code>, production G
        selection.
      </li>
      <li>
        Handling: <code>docs/specs/game/world/gravity-field/spec.md</code>,
        integration and resistance; star spec preserves handling and collisions.
      </li>
      <li>
        Art direction: <code>docs/design.md</code>, Intent and Art direction.
      </li>
      <li>
        Ownership finding: <code>apps/web/src/data/studies.ts</code>, the two
        stellar entries;
        <code
          >apps/web/src/pages/lab/studies/stellar-encounters-2026-11-11.astro</code
        >, opening and scope.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Not checked by the reviewer: rendered layout, keyboard operation, browser
      behaviour, future candidates’ scientific validity, visual quality,
      gameplay comprehension, balance, readiness or delivery feasibility. No
      files were edited and no automated checks were run by the reviewer.
    </p>
  </section>
</StudyLayout>
